Even before I had ascended at all, I preferred to play each game as if to
win (or do as well as possible) in _that_ game, not to play as if I wanted
to win _a_ game. I don't believe in early gambles like indiscriminate
fountain quaffing.

Of course in a game you find much tougher an early gamble can make sense
even from this point of view - in POWDER I will always try on the first
amulet I find because I expect the character to die without some positive
luck - but a suicide strategy obviously never makes sense.
